WEBVTT

01:35.804 --> 01:37.931
THE BEGINNING

01:38.014 --> 01:43.937
ALL THAT GLITTERS...

01:45.563 --> 01:47.857
- We've arrived.
- This is the place.

01:47.941 --> 01:49.442
It's huge!

01:49.526 --> 01:53.446
So this is the landlady's mansion.

01:53.530 --> 01:58.451
Now we'll somehow make it look
like the landlady died at home.

01:59.035 --> 02:04.249
Because things will get messy
if En finds out she died at our place.

02:05.792 --> 02:07.710
Saji, what are you doing?

02:07.794 --> 02:10.797
The embroidery side hustle
that is due today.

02:14.968 --> 02:17.220
There are security cameras installed!

02:17.303 --> 02:19.973
That rich woman! Damn it!

02:21.015 --> 02:23.476
Everyone, look over there.

02:26.437 --> 02:28.356
The security system's main unit.

02:28.439 --> 02:32.610
If we do something about it,
the security cameras should shut off.

02:33.111 --> 02:34.988
- Ton.
- Right.

02:41.703 --> 02:46.249
The distance to the target
is about 35 meters, isn't it?

02:48.084 --> 02:49.002
All right.

03:04.309 --> 03:08.730
Amazing! That was great, you pig!

03:10.064 --> 03:11.232
Passing through!

03:12.567 --> 03:16.571
Please insert smoke.

03:16.654 --> 03:18.656
So she had a smoke lock after all.

03:18.740 --> 03:21.743
It won't open
without the landlady's magic smoke.

03:22.327 --> 03:26.039
What should we do, Dokuga?
It's not like we can waste time here.

03:26.122 --> 03:27.248
Okay!

03:27.332 --> 03:30.084
I guess it is my turn to shine!

03:50.230 --> 03:52.357
How do you like my crazy strength?

03:52.941 --> 03:53.900
Amazing!

03:53.983 --> 03:57.278
I don't really care,
but let's hurry and get in.

03:57.362 --> 03:59.989
It's so dark
that I can't do my embroidery.

04:00.073 --> 04:02.492
Really, what the hell did you come for?

04:02.575 --> 04:04.369
So heavy...

04:05.245 --> 04:07.664
She must weigh about 400 kilos!

04:07.747 --> 04:10.375
It's so spacious here.
Is this the entryway?

04:10.458 --> 04:13.169
Dammit. Let's steal something
on our way home.

04:13.753 --> 04:15.421
Like toilet paper and stuff.

04:17.006 --> 04:21.010
Looking at this makes me feel guilty.

04:21.094 --> 04:24.764
Let's hurry and fake
the landlady's natural death.

04:27.141 --> 04:32.188
One of the most frequent deaths at home
is drowning in the bathtub.

04:36.234 --> 04:38.194
The water temperature is great.

04:38.278 --> 04:41.781
Wait just a little more... Damn it!

04:43.283 --> 04:44.284
Got it off!

04:46.494 --> 04:48.037
So heavy...

04:54.794 --> 04:56.254
Not very natural.

05:00.633 --> 05:04.012
If we tie a rope around her neck
and drop her from here,

05:04.095 --> 05:05.930
it'll look like suicide.

05:06.764 --> 05:08.558
Dokuga, did you write it?

05:08.641 --> 05:09.642
Yeah.

05:12.312 --> 05:13.521
Pretty natural, right?

05:14.605 --> 05:17.025
Hey! We're throwing her down!

05:17.108 --> 05:18.651
Do it.

05:18.735 --> 05:19.819
One, two...

05:19.902 --> 05:23.865
Hey, Dokuga. Who killed Risu?

05:24.365 --> 05:25.783
Is it someone we know?

05:28.494 --> 05:30.121
So heavy...

05:30.204 --> 05:35.251
Also, you failed to kill Risu.
Is that true?

05:36.044 --> 05:37.503
Yeah, it's true.

05:37.587 --> 05:40.381
Don't talk nonsense.
You could do it just fine.

05:47.680 --> 05:48.556
The problem...

05:50.683 --> 05:53.561
The problem is Risu's magic.

05:54.479 --> 05:56.939
Risu's magic?

05:59.776 --> 06:01.527
Dokuga!

06:06.032 --> 06:07.200
Dokuga!

06:16.584 --> 06:20.588
What the hell is that?!

06:23.383 --> 06:24.550
Dokuga!

06:29.847 --> 06:33.768
I know about this thing.
It's a diet insect.

06:33.851 --> 06:37.522
If you keep them in your stomach,
they absorb whatever you eat.

06:37.605 --> 06:40.775
So it came out
after the landlady died? Well...

06:40.858 --> 06:43.152
This looks pretty natural to me.

06:43.236 --> 06:44.654
What part of it?

06:44.737 --> 06:45.696
Dokuga!

06:45.780 --> 06:48.324
- Let's grab what we can and run.
- Keep it together!

06:48.408 --> 06:51.035
I've finally finished my embroidery.

06:51.619 --> 06:55.039
I hope it becomes the handkerchief
of a lovely lady.

06:55.123 --> 06:56.416
Hurry up and move!

06:57.667 --> 07:00.044
Whoa! What wonderful embroidery!

07:00.128 --> 07:04.674
It's so nice that girls can have
this kind of cute underwear.

07:07.635 --> 07:12.932
This is a nameless store
near the entrance to Hell.

07:13.015 --> 07:14.434
CUTE BUTCHER

07:20.940 --> 07:23.192
What kind of store is this?

07:23.276 --> 07:25.445
It's a store that sells meat.

07:25.528 --> 07:27.947
But I don't see the store owner anywhere.

07:28.030 --> 07:32.285
You just can't see him
because you're still a Devil trainee.

07:32.368 --> 07:34.328
Look, you can see his shadow.

07:35.246 --> 07:37.832
He isn't a Devil or a Sorcerer,

07:37.915 --> 07:40.376
and neither good nor evil.

07:43.713 --> 07:45.131
Give me some meat.

07:49.427 --> 07:51.387
What's this meat?

07:52.638 --> 07:54.432
The meat of a certain creature.

07:54.515 --> 07:58.352
Once you eat it,
your body will start turning into a Devil.

08:06.068 --> 08:08.196
Yeah. I'm counting on you.

08:10.323 --> 08:15.244
Asu, you kept a secret from us,
your comrades.

08:16.078 --> 08:18.748
That's something I can't forgive.

08:19.415 --> 08:24.879
I just called Store to come.
Do you understand what that means, Asu?

08:42.605 --> 08:45.608
You're a failure of a Devil, Asu.

09:10.007 --> 09:12.927
Okay, Store. Do it.

09:49.505 --> 09:52.758
Here, Store. Take it.

09:56.220 --> 09:59.265
Asu, you're an idiot.

10:00.516 --> 10:05.313
No, you're not Asu anymore.
Kawajiri the Sorcerer, wasn't it?

10:07.398 --> 10:12.653
See you, Kawajiri.
You can live as you please as a Sorcerer.

10:17.158 --> 10:21.662
My Devil power is fading out.

10:21.746 --> 10:24.248
Nikaido...

10:28.419 --> 10:29.754
EAST ZAGAN
TORQUE

10:29.837 --> 10:31.088
How about it?

10:31.172 --> 10:36.761
Does anyone want some freshly baked bread
loaded with cheese and a creamy stew?

10:36.844 --> 10:39.347
- Please give me three!
- Thank you.

10:43.934 --> 10:46.937
You're really eating with your mask on.

10:47.021 --> 10:50.983
So I'm the one paying, Big Bro?

10:54.987 --> 10:57.239
- Delicious!
- This is amazing!

11:05.831 --> 11:10.753
How about it?
Does anyone want some creamy stew?

11:13.339 --> 11:16.258
NEW MEAT SHIPMENT ARRIVED!

11:20.388 --> 11:25.810
The night before
I turned Asu back into a Sorcerer.

11:27.311 --> 11:30.314
As I thought,
my own mask calms me down the most.

11:30.398 --> 11:32.900
This is bad! It's already this late.

11:32.983 --> 11:34.944
I need to sleep soon.

11:35.486 --> 11:41.158
Still, I need to hide this mask
in a place that is harder to find.

11:41.242 --> 11:44.662
Hiding it under the drawer
is too obvious and dangerous.

11:45.329 --> 11:47.248
Maybe inside the closet?

11:50.751 --> 11:54.672
What's this? A notebook?
Could it be Nikaido's?

11:55.548 --> 11:57.466
A smoke lock.

11:58.718 --> 12:00.511
Let's open it!

12:00.594 --> 12:03.556
A lock like this
is nothing against my magic!

12:08.269 --> 12:10.688
MY HEART'S DIARY

12:11.272 --> 12:13.524
"My heart's diary."

12:14.191 --> 12:17.194
That bitch has zero naming sense!

12:17.278 --> 12:18.696
Let's see.

12:18.779 --> 12:21.407
I feel like the power
of the Devil's contract

12:21.490 --> 12:23.075
is about to crush me.

12:23.159 --> 12:26.787
At this rate, I may disappear.

12:26.871 --> 12:31.083
But before that,
I'll write about my magic in this diary.

12:32.918 --> 12:36.172
So even if the contract
controls me completely,

12:36.255 --> 12:38.340
I never use my magic.

12:38.424 --> 12:40.259
DOOR TO THE PAST

12:43.137 --> 12:46.307
I grew up in a small village
deep in the mountains.

12:46.390 --> 12:50.060
It seems that my parents passed away
when I was a baby.

12:50.144 --> 12:52.688
But I was happy.

12:53.189 --> 12:55.357
I had a kind uncle and auntie,

12:55.441 --> 12:59.445
and Kawajiri, who cared for me
just like a real big brother would do.

12:59.945 --> 13:01.572
Every day was fun.

13:02.740 --> 13:06.035
Until Yakumo, my best friend, disappeared.

13:07.161 --> 13:08.704
That's it, I'm too sleepy.

13:09.288 --> 13:11.207
I'll read the rest tomorrow.

13:14.585 --> 13:17.546
I want to hear your opinion
on a new product

13:17.630 --> 13:19.340
that will be sold under my brand.

13:19.423 --> 13:22.885
Its name is the "En-Shaped Mushroom Doll."

13:22.968 --> 13:25.846
It's an edible mushroom pet for my fans.

13:25.930 --> 13:27.932
It's amazing, En!

13:28.432 --> 13:31.560
It reacts to humidity and airflow.

13:31.644 --> 13:35.272
So cute! Give me one.

13:36.440 --> 13:39.568
Their tendency
to parasitize other creatures

13:39.652 --> 13:42.071
still needs some improvement.

13:42.154 --> 13:45.616
What do you think, Nikaido?
Let me hear your opinion.

13:45.699 --> 13:49.578
Let's see. I think it would be better
if they were bigger.

13:49.662 --> 13:51.831
Like the same size as you, En.

13:51.914 --> 13:54.583
Nice opinion, Nikaido! Approved!

13:54.667 --> 13:55.835
Hurray!

13:55.918 --> 13:59.380
Stop it! Someone take it off of me!

14:00.506 --> 14:04.635
By the way, Nikaido.
You're still not ready to use magic?

14:05.219 --> 14:06.929
I hate talking about that.

14:07.012 --> 14:11.308
Nikaido, wait!
I wasn't planning on forcing you.

14:11.892 --> 14:13.102
Nikaido...

14:15.813 --> 14:17.565
That caught me by surprise.

14:17.648 --> 14:21.569
I guess pretending to get mad
and running away won't work anymore.

14:22.236 --> 14:24.071
That made me sweat.

14:24.154 --> 14:27.199
Let's take a bath
and keep reading that diary.

14:29.910 --> 14:32.329
Let's see.

14:32.413 --> 14:38.460
"I was able to first use magic
when I was two or three years old."

14:40.421 --> 14:42.590
You're amazing, Nikaido.

14:47.094 --> 14:49.555
- What's this?
- Candy?

14:49.638 --> 14:54.268
We may find out once you're able
to make more and more smoke.

14:54.351 --> 14:56.312
Nikaido will do her best!

14:56.395 --> 14:57.771
Hey!

14:57.855 --> 15:00.274
Kawajiri! Nikaido!

15:00.357 --> 15:01.483
Yakumo!

15:02.109 --> 15:05.446
Yakumo's magic was the power
to fly through the sky.

15:06.947 --> 15:08.699
When she was a baby,

15:08.782 --> 15:12.119
she happened to be rescued
while floating down the river.

15:12.202 --> 15:16.457
Because of that,
she used to say she was a lucky one.

15:17.875 --> 15:21.629
She was a fearless and cheerful girl.

15:24.757 --> 15:27.426
- Isn't that a child's corpse?
- Scary!

15:27.509 --> 15:32.181
There must be some hunters nearby.
Let's hurry and go home.

15:32.264 --> 15:36.936
The hunters were a group
that kidnapped Sorcerer kids.

15:37.603 --> 15:42.066
There were many kids who died
because of fights between hunters.

15:42.650 --> 15:43.901
Hey, young man.

15:44.401 --> 15:48.364
Leave the children here and go.
One of mine just died, you know?

15:48.447 --> 15:49.323
It's a hunter!

15:49.406 --> 15:52.326
You asshole! Punch!

15:58.791 --> 16:00.209
They disappeared!

16:01.001 --> 16:05.756
Kawajiri was a Sorcerer with magic
that allowed him to go anywhere.

16:06.256 --> 16:08.133
He also had clairvoyance

16:08.217 --> 16:10.678
and could apparently
choose locations freely.

16:11.178 --> 16:12.346
I'm home, Auntie.

16:13.430 --> 16:17.685
Kawajiri. Stop relying on magic
for everything

16:17.768 --> 16:19.353
and walk a little bit more.

16:19.436 --> 16:20.562
He's right.

16:20.646 --> 16:22.731
We just escaped from a hunter.

16:22.815 --> 16:25.359
Woo-hoo! Today we're eating gyoza!

16:25.442 --> 16:28.737
Gyoza were Auntie's specialty.

16:28.821 --> 16:31.031
I wonder what gyoza are.

16:31.115 --> 16:35.744
I'm not really familiar
with the food of commoners.

16:36.328 --> 16:39.248
And then, when I was around four...

16:41.959 --> 16:43.627
What are you two doing?

16:43.711 --> 16:47.965
Welcome home, Kawajiri.
I was training Nikaido just now.

16:48.048 --> 16:50.259
I can break boards now.

16:50.342 --> 16:52.845
Aren't you bleeding?

16:52.928 --> 16:54.513
This is too much, Yakumo.

16:54.596 --> 16:58.058
That's how her fists will get stronger.

16:58.851 --> 16:59.768
What's that?

17:01.770 --> 17:02.771
This is...

17:04.440 --> 17:08.027
I got it the other day
from a Devil who gave me his card.

17:08.110 --> 17:10.279
It seems he made it specially for me.

17:10.362 --> 17:11.280
So cool!

17:12.614 --> 17:15.034
He invited me to become a Devil.

17:25.627 --> 17:28.047
Do your best, Kawajiri.

17:28.130 --> 17:31.300
That's some impressive armor.
You okay in there?

17:31.383 --> 17:36.847
Yeah. It seems living ordinarily
while wearing this is the first training.

17:37.347 --> 17:39.725
Well, then, I'm leaving for work.

17:40.601 --> 17:42.728
There's no point if he doesn't walk.

17:43.520 --> 17:47.733
That day, I looked after the house
by myself for the first time.

17:47.816 --> 17:52.780
Once I finished helping wrap the gyoza,
I suddenly had nothing to do.

17:55.157 --> 17:59.411
I decided to use magic again
after a long time

17:59.495 --> 18:01.288
by trying to produce some smoke.

18:04.374 --> 18:07.586
Maybe my magic power
had increased as I got older,

18:07.669 --> 18:11.006
but the cube was about half my size.

18:12.174 --> 18:14.968
The cube had buttons and levers on it.

18:15.052 --> 18:19.723
And while I tried pressing and pulling
them randomly, nothing really happened.

18:20.682 --> 18:25.938
I decided to practice
in order to master my magic.

18:29.608 --> 18:34.363
I didn't know that would be
the beginning of a frightening event.

18:34.446 --> 18:36.365
- Nikaido!
- It's En!

18:36.448 --> 18:38.367
Open the door! It's me!

18:38.450 --> 18:41.620
I came to apologize.
I also brought you presents.

18:41.703 --> 18:44.373
Just when things were getting interesting.

18:44.456 --> 18:46.458
I need to dry my hair.

18:46.959 --> 18:47.960
What?

18:50.712 --> 18:51.755
What the hell?

18:52.840 --> 18:57.970
What?! You mean you really don't know
where the Cross-Eyes' hideout is?

18:58.053 --> 19:02.641
Sorry. I couldn't help it.
I just really wanted to go with you.

19:02.724 --> 19:05.978
But we'll find it right away
if we look for it.

19:06.061 --> 19:08.147
Look for it?

19:08.230 --> 19:10.357
But we don't have any information.

19:10.440 --> 19:12.151
It's gonna get dark soon.

19:12.234 --> 19:14.945
Then let's rest somewhere tonight.

19:15.028 --> 19:17.656
Let's start looking
for the hideout tomorrow.

19:19.533 --> 19:21.410
Are you fine with that, Caiman?

19:24.037 --> 19:26.415
Yeah, sure.

19:27.416 --> 19:28.625
Caiman.

19:30.002 --> 19:34.256
But is there a place we can stay
in such a backwater?

19:34.339 --> 19:37.676
Well, this place's good enough, isn't it?

19:37.759 --> 19:40.679
BERITH HOT SPRINGS

19:40.762 --> 19:43.182
Welcome!

19:43.265 --> 19:46.685
Three customers have arrived!

19:48.770 --> 19:52.024
A married couple and their child?

19:52.900 --> 19:54.818
MAGMA BATH

19:54.902 --> 19:57.821
- Won't you open, please, Nikaido?
- What should I do?

19:57.905 --> 20:00.199
- Nikaido!
- I suddenly turned back to normal.

20:02.910 --> 20:05.329
Ouch! What?

20:05.412 --> 20:07.748
What's wrong, Nikaido? Are you okay?

20:07.831 --> 20:12.085
Is this the contract from En
that was inside Nikaido's body?

20:16.006 --> 20:17.090
Nikaido!

20:18.926 --> 20:21.678
Nikaido, I'm sorry about earlier.

20:21.762 --> 20:24.848
I forgive you.

20:24.932 --> 20:28.560
Chota! You damn bird!
What do you think you're doing?

20:28.644 --> 20:30.854
There's a reason for this!

20:31.730 --> 20:32.606
What?

20:33.273 --> 20:36.360
Nikaido ran away with that lizard man?

20:36.443 --> 20:38.612
Then the Nikaido that was here recently...

20:38.695 --> 20:40.614
Sorry, that was me.

20:40.697 --> 20:42.366
Turn into mushrooms!

20:42.950 --> 20:44.701
I'm sorry!

20:52.209 --> 20:53.961
It's so noisy inside the mansion.

20:54.461 --> 20:58.924
Anyway, where the hell did Ebisu go?

20:59.007 --> 21:01.969
Just when I got my salary
from the Big Boss.

21:02.052 --> 21:03.553
It's not much, though.

21:05.222 --> 21:09.893
Well, she isn't an official member
of the family anyway.

21:09.977 --> 21:12.271
Somehow she ended up staying here.

21:12.354 --> 21:14.982
Now may be a good time to kick her out.

21:16.108 --> 21:17.401
Ebisu?

21:19.486 --> 21:21.530
Where is she going?

21:21.613 --> 21:23.407
And with all that luggage.

21:24.533 --> 21:27.160
Could it be that she's planning to leave?

21:30.080 --> 21:33.166
Let her leave if she wants to.
That cold-hearted jerk.

21:35.002 --> 21:36.295
Ebisu!

21:43.343 --> 21:45.387
Where are you going?

21:45.887 --> 21:47.180
I'm going home.

21:47.264 --> 21:51.560
Home? Did you get your memories back?

23:30.659 --> 23:31.910
THE END

23:31.993 --> 23:33.954
What we learned in Episode 4.

23:34.037 --> 23:36.665
Store sells a certain creature's meat.

23:36.748 --> 23:38.250
Natsuki is the one who pays.

23:38.333 --> 23:39.918
En found out many things.

23:40.001 --> 23:43.880
What we'll learn in Episode 5
is still hidden in chaos.

23:43.964 --> 23:46.925
This is Dorohedoro.
